 LINE  ADDR  CODE         SOURCE
    1                     ; OCR transcription of docs/scans/lander.pdf ("Lander" game, QUESTDATA
    2                     ; COSMAC CLUB, pages 4-5). Flowcharts on these pages are NOT transcribed
    3                     ; (per instructions); their logic corresponds to the shift/clamp loop in
    4                     ; the Input/Move Subroutine around 0539-0573, noted there as a comment.
    5                     ;
    6                     ; METHODOLOGY: this listing's "Code" column is the authoritative source
    7                     ; for every operand (register number, immediate byte, branch target);
    8                     ; the "Mnem." column only names the instruction family, with NO operand
    9                     ; text (unlike the PD1802 listing transcribed earlier). Every operand
   10                     ; below was decoded by hand from the printed hex bytes against the
   11                     ; standard CDP1802 opcode map (register-implied: 0N/1N/2N/4N/5N/8N/9N/
   12                     ; AN/BN/DN/EN; branches 30-3F; INP 69-6F/OUT 61-67; ALU F0-FF). Loc is
   13                     ; used to place ORG directives (per instructions), including at the one
   14                     ; place the listing itself skips addresses (045C-046F, unlisted) and
   15                     ; wherever a new named subroutine starts on a different page/column than
   16                     ; the previous one ends, since this listing's sections are NOT printed
   17                     ; in memory order (Display Subroutine, at 04CE, is printed on page 5
   18                     ; after Draw Subroutine at 0580, which is itself after Input/Move at
   19                     ; 0500+, even though 04CE < 0500 < 0580 in memory).
   20                     ;
   21                     ; Short-branch targets (2-byte opcode, low byte in Code) were computed as
   22                     ; (page of the branch instruction itself) | (low byte in Code), per the
   23                     ; 1802 short-branch rule, and given address-named labels (L<loc>) purely
   24                     ; for traceability back to the original Loc column -- cross-check any of
   25                     ; them directly against the scan by looking up that address.
   26                     ;
   27                     ; One OCR uncertainty worth re-checking against the original scan: at
   28                     ; 0552 the Code/Mnem are transcribed literally as "AB"/"PLO" (PLO RB),
   29                     ; but the mirrored Up/Down-movement block eight lines earlier (0531-
   30                     ; 0532) does the analogous step as "BB"/PHI" (PHI RB) -- the Left/Right
   31                     ; block otherwise mirrors the Up/Down block instruction-for-instruction,
   32                     ; so "BB PHI" is what's structurally expected here too. Transcribed as
   33                     ; literally read; flagged rather than silently corrected.
   34                     ;
   35                     ; Where the Code column shows two single-byte opcodes on one printed
   36                     ; line (common for runs of register-implied ops, e.g. "B1 B2" for two
   37                     ; separate PHI's), both are transcribed as separate instructions at
   38                     ; consecutive addresses, since the Mnem's own operand register differs
   39                     ; between them.
